Wine 11.18 nondefault window-bridge foundation.

Keep the existing default-device entry points for Vulkan and add constructors
which retain the caller-supplied renderer device. Reject a cached view or an
existing surface swapchain using another device, without altering its owner.
Check surface/view allocation before dereferencing and release partial state.

This does not publish the legacy macdrv_functions ABI or enable foreign-child
swapchains. Full window/CEF and supplied-device runtime acceptance remain open.

